yet|up-to-now|ADVERB|up to the present time|Used in a question or negative statement about something expected to happen by now.|chưa; cho đến lúc này|Have you checked the revised timetable yet?|Bạn đã kiểm tra thời gian biểu đã chỉnh sửa chưa?|Often at the end of a question or negative clause; not yet. Present perfect is common but not obligatory in every variety.|0
yet|contrast|CONJUNCTION|introducing a contrast|Used to connect two facts that seem surprising when considered together.|nhưng; tuy vậy|The room was small, yet everyone found a comfortable seat.|Căn phòng nhỏ, nhưng mọi người đều tìm được chỗ ngồi thoải mái.|Coordinating conjunction; a comma commonly precedes yet when it connects two independent clauses.|1
comply|follow-requirements|VERB|follow a rule or request|To act as a rule, instruction or request requires.|tuân thủ; chấp hành|All exhibitors must comply with the hall's safety instructions.|Tất cả người tham gia trưng bày phải tuân thủ hướng dẫn an toàn của hội trường.|Intransitive; comply with something, not comply something. Complied and complying are the inflected forms.|0
high|far-above-ground|ADJECTIVE|far above the ground|Extending far upwards or located far above the ground.|cao; ở trên cao|A high wall separated the garden from the busy road.|Một bức tường cao ngăn khu vườn với con đường đông đúc.|High wall or high shelf; higher, highest. Tall is commonly used for people's height.|0
high|at-great-height|ADVERB|at a great height|At a position far above the ground or another reference point.|ở trên cao; lên cao|The kite rose high above the roofs.|Cánh diều bay lên cao phía trên những mái nhà.|Fly high, climb high; higher and highest also function as adverbs. Highly usually expresses degree rather than physical height.|1
high|peak-level|NOUN|highest level reached|A particularly high level reached by something that changes over time.|mức cao; mức cao nhất đạt được|Attendance reached a new high during the summer exhibition.|Lượng người tham dự đạt mức cao mới trong triển lãm mùa hè.|Countable: a new high, an all-time high. The metric and time period should be clear.|2
inflate|fill-with-air|VERB|fill with air|To put air or another gas into something so that it becomes larger or firmer.|bơm phồng|The mechanic inflated the bicycle tyre before checking the valve.|Người thợ bơm phồng lốp xe đạp trước khi kiểm tra van.|Transitive inflate a tyre; also intransitive the tyre inflated. This draft concerns filling with gas, not price inflation.|-
prescribe|order-medicine|VERB|order a medical treatment|To officially recommend a medicine or treatment as a qualified medical professional.|kê đơn; chỉ định điều trị|The doctor prescribed a treatment after examining the patient.|Bác sĩ chỉ định điều trị sau khi khám người bệnh.|Transitive; prescribe something for someone. Prescribe is different from describe; no dose is specified here.|0
prescribe|lay-down-a-rule|VERB|state what must be done|To officially state a rule or requirement that people must follow.|quy định|The competition rules prescribe the size of every submitted model.|Thể lệ cuộc thi quy định kích thước của từng mô hình dự thi.|Formal transitive use; prescribe a method or requirement; prescribe that something be done.|1
